# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. Never tracked. `.env.example` is the template that IS tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
*.pem
*.key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Patient data and everything derived from it.
#
# `outputs/` is a scratch directory: the cohort CSV, every sub-CSV the data
# stage cuts from it, the matcher's column catalogue (all 1,394 names), and one
# folder per run. None of it belongs in a repository, and all of it is
# regenerable — see prep_hiv_dataset.py, make_sample_data.py, prep_nhanes.py and
# scripts/build_matcher_cache.py.
#
# The two entries below are the exceptions: the README explaining the folder,
# and the .gitkeep that keeps the empty folder present after a clone.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
outputs/*
!outputs/.gitkeep
!outputs/README.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Knowledge-graph dumps. AlzKB and AddictionKB are published elsewhere; these
# are 1GB of exports and their SQLite builds. The scripts that produce and read
# them are tracked, the payloads are not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
kg/**/*.db
kg/**/*.cypherl

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reinstallable
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv
.venv/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The rule files, which the global ignore would otherwise swallow.
#

# the grounds that it is local-only assistant tooling. In this repository it is
# not. These five files are the rules themselves — they cite line numbers that
# `scripts/check_citations.py` verifies on every run, and a citation in an
# untracked file is never checked, because the checker indexes `git ls-files`.
# `CLAUDE_KR.md` is a tracked Korean edition like `BACKLOG_KR.md`.
#
# ASAREE and motoro both track theirs, and are unaffected by the global rule
# only because a file already tracked stays tracked. This repository has to say
# so out loud. The negation is deliberately un-anchored, so it covers the three

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS and Office leavings
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
~$*
